<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Mac App Store: APP SANDBOX, which is mandatory there.

  Deliberately NOT a copy of direct.entitlements. The two hardened-runtime
  allowances that build needs are the ones App Review scrutinises hardest, and
  a sandboxed store build should not be asking for either.

  What is requested, and why each is genuinely needed:

    * app-sandbox — required for the Mac App Store. Not optional.

    * network.client — OUTBOUND ONLY. The app calls Anthropic on the user's
      own key and the Dawnlist feed service. There is deliberately no
      network.server: nothing listens.

    * files.user-selected.read-only — the user adds CVs through the open
      panel or by dragging them onto the window. Read-only is correct: the
      app never writes back to a file the user picked. Asking for read-write
      would be a larger claim than the app can justify.

  What is NOT requested, and must stay that way:

    * No downloads or desktop folder access. The database, drafts and voice
      samples live in the app's own container, which needs no entitlement.
    * No com.apple.security.files.bookmarks — the app does not need to reopen
      a file across launches; it reads a CV once and keeps what it extracted.
    * No network.server, no camera, no microphone, no location, no address
      book, no print. The app uses none of them.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-only</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
